@startuml SSD-HandleReturns
' ===========================================================================
' POS System - System Sequence Diagram: Handle Returns (main success scenario)
' Software Engineering Practice - Part 2, artifact 1 (third element)
'
' Modelled by analogy with Process Sale ("比着葫芦画瓢"): the same shape of
' transaction, with the events that the Handle Returns use case text implies.
' ===========================================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #1F4E79
  ActorBorderColor #1F4E79
  ActorBackgroundColor #DEEAF6
  LifeLineBorderColor #1F4E79
  ParticipantBorderColor #1F4E79
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #DEEAF6
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #D6B656
}

actor "Cashier" as Cashier
participant ":System" as System

activate System

Cashier -> System : makeNewReturn(originalSaleID)
activate System
System --> Cashier : «create» a return

Cashier -> System : enterReturnItem(itemID, quantity, resellable)
System --> Cashier : description, refund amount

Cashier -> System : enterReturnItem(itemID, quantity, resellable)
System --> Cashier : description, refund amount

Cashier -> System : getRefundTotal()
System --> Cashier : refund total

Cashier -> System : authorizeRefund(method)
System --> Cashier : refund authorised

Cashier -> System : endReturn()
System --> Cashier : refund receipt

deactivate System
deactivate System

note right of System
  **System events**: makeNewReturn, enterReturnItem,
  getRefundTotal, authorizeRefund, endReturn.

  Events 2-4 may repeat for each returned item.
end note


' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Alternate scenarios (documented in full in the fully dressed use case text,
' not on this SSD, which shows the main success scenario only):
'
'   3a. The item id is not found on the original sale.
'   3b. The returned quantity exceeds the quantity sold on that receipt.
'   5a. The card refund is rejected by the issuer -> reimburse in cash instead.
'   1a. No receipt is available -> return without a link to the original sale.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@enduml
